{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-pair-nonneg","title":"lem:busemann-pair-nonneg","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":1032,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#lem:busemann-pair-nonneg","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-function]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-approx]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"lem:busemann-pair-nonneg","line":1654,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[The Busemann pair of a line is non-negative]\n\\label{lem:busemann-pair-nonneg}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:busemann-function, def:minimizing-geodesic-window}\n\n\n\n\n\nFor the Busemann pair of a minimizing line,\n$$B_+(x)+B_-(x)\\ge0\\qquad(x\\in M).$$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{def:busemann-approx}\nFor $s,t\\ge0$, the triangle inequality between $\\lambda(-s)$,\n$x$, and $\\lambda(t)$ gives\n$B_{\\lambda_+,t}(x)+B_{\\lambda_-,s}(x)\\ge0$. Take both infima.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[The Busemann pair of a line is non-negative] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a627573656d616e6e2d706169722d6e6f6e6e6567\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">morgan-tian</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Abusemann-function\">↗ def:busemann-function</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aminimizing-geodesic-window\">↗ def:minimizing-geodesic-window</a> <p></p>For the Busemann pair of a minimizing line, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[ B_+(x)+B_-(x)\\ge 0\\qquad (x\\in M). \\]\">\\[ B_+(x)+B_-(x)\\ge 0\\qquad (x\\in M). \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Abusemann-approx\">↗ def:busemann-approx</a> For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s,t\\ge 0$\">$s,t\\ge 0$</span>, the triangle inequality between <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda (-s)$\">$\\lambda (-s)$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda (t)$\">$\\lambda (t)$</span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_{\\lambda _+,t}(x)+B_{\\lambda _-,s}(x)\\ge 0$\">$B_{\\lambda _+,t}(x)+B_{\\lambda _-,s}(x)\\ge 0$</span>. Take both infima. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-along-line","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#cor:busemann-pair-vanishes-on-line","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-function","title":"def:busemann-function","label":"def:busemann-function"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","label":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-approx","title":"def:busemann-approx","label":"def:busemann-approx"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#line","title":"line","label":"line"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-pair-nonneg","title":"lem:busemann-pair-nonneg","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[The Busemann pair of a line is non-negative]\n\\label{lem:busemann-pair-nonneg}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:busemann-function, def:minimizing-geodesic-window}\n\n\n\n\n\nFor the Busemann pair of a minimizing line,\n$$B_+(x)+B_-(x)\\ge0\\qquad(x\\in M).$$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{def:busemann-approx}\nFor $s,t\\ge0$, the triangle inequality between $\\lambda(-s)$,\n$x$, and $\\lambda(t)$ gives\n$B_{\\lambda_+,t}(x)+B_{\\lambda_-,s}(x)\\ge0$. Take both infima.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-function","title":"def:busemann-function","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-approx","title":"def:busemann-approx","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}